  "kanji": "札",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 札\ntitle: tag; banknote\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [サツ]\nkunyomi: [ふだ]\ndistractors: [礼, 机, 村]\n---\n\n# 札 — tag; banknote\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n札 can name a tag, label, card, or banknote. The reading depends on the word: 札 さつ is a banknote, while 札 ふだ has uses such as a ticket, tag, or charm.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice 木 beside the short right-hand hook and imagine a small tag hanging from a wooden object. This is a modern-shape memory aid, not etymology.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| サツ | on | [札](../words/札.md) さつ - banknote; bill |\n| ふだ | kun | 札 ふだ - ticket; tag; charm |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [札](../words/札.md) さつ - banknote; bill\n- 札 ふだ - ticket; tag\n- [改札](../words/改札.md) かいさつ - ticket inspection; ticket gate\n\n## Notes\n\n- The linked 札 article teaches さつ, banknote. The separate ふだ entry is retained here without linking it as if it were that article's primary reading.\n- Do not infer the pronunciation of an unfamiliar word merely from the physical object looking like a card. Learn the complete word and its reading.\n- 札 ふだ can also name a charm or talisman; this does not make every banknote a religious object.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1200840, 1298960, 1298970.\n",
